From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:17:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0093: the NGG prologue's EXEC is true in wave64
 vertex shaders (P4, piece 1)

Kyty gives a vertex shader its lane count in s3: the popcount of the entry Ballot(true), | 1 << 28
(Translate.cpp). The game's NGG prologue turns it back into EXEC = -1 >> ((K - s3) & 63), K = 0 (Astro
Bot, Tekken 8, Clair Obscur, Wukong) or K = 64 with s3 & 0xff (FF7 Remake, KH3), and Kyty translates
that EXEC into a test of each lane's bit (ThreadBit). LaneMaskProjection folded such tests in wave32
only, from Ballot and LiveMask. In the six games' 0092 caches, these tests drive 38 to 74% of the
selects of the vertex shaders.

- Lane L's bit of that mask is set exactly when L < n. The host lanes of a vertex wave are packed from
  lane 0, which this EXEC already assumes (a lane at or above n would drop its vertex): in a wave64
  vertex shader, a lane test whose two words are the halves of that prefix folds to true, and every
  VGPR write under it loses its select.
- The count has to be the entry block's s3 itself, or s3 & m with the low six bits of m set, and K a
  multiple of 64. A count the guest computes, even from the entry EXEC words, or an s3 it wrote, keeps
  its test.
- ConstantPropagationPass takes the stage (the main passes, the call-target query, tessellation).
- --compile-only gains VertexNggPrologueExecFoldsToTrue: K = 0, K = 64 with s3 & 0xff in either operand
  order, and K = 0 through an SGPR pair fold; K = 32, s3 & 31, a guest count of EXEC | 1 << 28 and a
  guest-written s3 keep their lane test.

No vertex shader of the six games is wave32: the wave32 form is left as it was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
